schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Retroactive Public Goods Funding (RetroPGF / Retro Funding)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Funding that flips prospective funding's timing: instead of pitching a
    plan, a project ships work first, and a later round looks back and pays
    for what proved useful. The Optimism Collective runs the largest version.
  source_traditions:
    - Optimism Collective (850M OP reserved for public goods, 20% of supply)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Positioned as suiting nodes that already produce visible, attributable
    work rather than brand-new ones; hypercerts are presented as the
    evidentiary record that lets a retro round know what a node actually did.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - hypercerts (the structured impact record retro rounds are read against)
    - quadratic funding (the prospective counterpart in the article's "two families" framing)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      Retrospective (pays after impact is shown) vs. prospective (pays before
      the work happens) — the article's organizing distinction for the whole
      funding landscape.
  tensions:
    - >-
      "No proposal-writing theatre" relief vs. the risk of funding yourself
      out of pocket first and hoping a future round notices you.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Assuming retro funding suits any node, when the article is explicit it
    rewards track records and therefore suits established nodes, not
    brand-new ones.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/funding-landscape.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
